{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters","id":74341,"title":"Nothing \"Matters\".","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-18T09:52:42-08:00","id":74341,"title":"Nothing \"Matters\".","content":"I think I freaked some people out at work today. They were talking about the Olympics and they talked about these people training for 17 years or some such skating and they finally won a gold medal. My response was: &quot;Ok..so? Now what?&quot;. And they asked me how could I say that, these people just won the gold and were the best in the world at whatever it was. And I said, so what? They're &quot;the best in the world&quot; of the people that could show up for that. But so what if they're the best in the world at skating or whatever, what does it matter? And now what are they going to do?&quot;<br /> <br /> I might as well have been an alien. They couldn't understand why it wouldn't matter to me. And this started a whole long conversation about how I don't think anything we do &quot;matters&quot;? It might matter to you, or a small group of people, but ultimately nothing matters.<br /> <br /> There was also talk about people competing in things &quot;just to do it&quot; or &quot;just to say they did&quot;, and I blew their minds I guess because I'm not like that. I guess I don't have anything to prove or whatever, but I don't get it. If you want to do something &quot;just to do it&quot; why do you have compete to do it? If you want to run a marathon, why not just go out there and run the distance? Why do you have to do it sanctioned competitions and such? I know, people like to compete and show off for other people. But they like to pretend thats somehow important...<br /> <br /> But anyway, it was kind of funny to me. I guess that makes me sound super depressed or something, and in some ways I guess I am. But yea, things only &quot;matter&quot; in the right now. There is no grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just have a strange view of things I guess. Or I'm in a strange mood today...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:13:33-08:00","id":74356,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much my thinking...I don't get into all that stuff or want to go into competitions. I've liked keeping to myself and with family and friends and to them...I matter. To myself, that's what matters, that I'm happy just to do something for and around them and because I enjoy it.<br /> <br /> There was a time in high school where we had to write short stories and some were going to be chosen for a school-wide competition and mine ended up being one of those winners. I just wrote it in hopes of disturbing my teacher because I hated the assignment....and I won...? I got some money for it but didn't really &quot;feel&quot; anything from having one other than confusion as to why something like that was picked for sharing in a competition against the whole damn school...<br /> <br /> I hated that piece of work because I knew I could do a lot better but hated the assignment and didn't give my all because of it. It happened again on a smaller scale, writing for a health class and having to include vocabulary words. I couldn't think of something good in an hour that I'd actually 'want' to share, so made some stupid shit up that the vocabulary words didn't even mesh well with the bullshit story about a woman becoming a vampire and claiming her twin brother ( very very old bullshit idea for Rayvin Miyu back in the day ). I was one of about three in the class to get an A+ while others were getting B's and lower but had much better stories.... The teacher was so happy with my work and made notice to everyone in class about it but I just...uuugh.<br /> <br /> <br /> I look at sports shows and such in a similar way...I'm not amazed or even interested in them or how good just one player is. I don't see the point in them and in praising a person over and over for how great they are for a play when they're in a team but the whole of the team isn't talked about in a positive light...just the one or two players.... I just don't care about one single person &quot;at the top of their game&quot;... I hate Olympics because that's all it is, people wanting to be known for being number one...but for what? Possible contracts for jobs in teams, maybe? I don't know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i><span style=\"color:darkred\">Got an angel on the left hand and a devil on the right<br /> She's gonna raise a little hell up in heaven tonight---Vixen</span></i></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:olive\"><i>When you say it's all divine and meant to be<br /> What about your flesh and blood and defiers like me?---Avantasia</i></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/821-rayvin-miyu","name":"Rayvin Miyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:16:15-08:00","id":74360,"title":"","content":"Most people have personalities that drive them to want to believe things matter. It is a deep-set psychological need for the vast majority of humans and the number of people that can handle the idea that &quot;nothing matters&quot; and still be mentally healthy is probably at most a single digit of a percent of the human population. As such, most people, when not having to fight for survival on a daily basis, will turn trivial little things of monumental importance when they don't really matter at all (even if you believe things matter) such as sports. Sports is just a nearly universal accepted hobby that people love to make into a much bigger deal than it is. But then, you can find people who are like that in nearly every human endeavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:35:02-08:00","id":74369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayvin Miyu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74356#post74356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty much my thinking...I don't get into all that stuff or want to go into competitions. I've liked keeping to myself and with family and friends and to them...I matter. To myself, that's what matters, that I'm happy just to do something for and around them and because I enjoy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here pretty much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayvin Miyu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74356#post74356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a time in high school where we had to write short stories and some were going to be chosen for a school-wide competition and mine ended up being one of those winners. I just wrote it in hopes of disturbing my teacher because I hated the assignment....and I won...? I got some money for it but didn't really &quot;feel&quot; anything from having one other than confusion as to why something like that was picked for sharing in a competition against the whole damn school...<br /> <br /> I hated that piece of work because I knew I could do a lot better but hated the assignment and didn't give my all because of it. It happened again on a smaller scale, writing for a health class and having to include vocabulary words. I couldn't think of something good in an hour that I'd actually 'want' to share, so made some stupid shit up that the vocabulary words didn't even mesh well with the bullshit story about a woman becoming a vampire and claiming her twin brother ( very very old bullshit idea for Rayvin Miyu back in the day ). I was one of about three in the class to get an A+ while others were getting B's and lower but had much better stories.... The teacher was so happy with my work and made notice to everyone in class about it but I just...uuugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Thats usually the way it goes... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bet it pissed everyone who really cared about it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayvin Miyu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74356#post74356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look at sports shows and such in a similar way...I'm not amazed or even interested in them or how good just one player is. I don't see the point in them and in praising a person over and over for how great they are for a play when they're in a team but the whole of the team isn't talked about in a positive light...just the one or two players.... I just don't care about one single person &quot;at the top of their game&quot;... I hate Olympics because that's all it is, people wanting to be known for being number one...but for what? Possible contracts for jobs in teams, maybe? I don't know...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally with you on that. And I don't understand it. You do all this work, but then what does it all matter when you're done. I guess with sports teams and such you get paid millions of dollars(which is a whole other amount of bullshit I don't get at all) so you have that going for you if you're &quot;better&quot; than some people, but even then, it's a game you play with a team. So like you said, why do people get all focused on one player?<br /> <br /> And yea, with the Olympics, I just don't get it. Theres billions of people in the world. I'd be willing to bet there is someone else out there better at whatever then the handful of people who go to the Olympics. Plus, as with most sports, just because you were the best at that exact minute doesn't mean you would be 5 minutes later. Alot of it is factors beyond people's controls and you just happen to have to pefect circumstances that allowed you to do a hair better than the other people trying. Luck I suppose...<br /> <br /> But yea, you spend all this time, years, trying to prove something, but once you do it, then what? You've spent years of your life so you can &quot;better&quot; at something for a small amount of time. But then what do you?<br /> <br /> Of course it could be said I haven't done anything for that same amount of time and I have nothing to show for it. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74360#post74360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people have personalities that drive them to want to believe things matter. It is a deep-set psychological need for the vast majority of humans and the number of people that can handle the idea that &quot;nothing matters&quot; and still be mentally healthy is probably at most a single digit of a percent of the human population. As such, most people, when not having to fight for survival on a daily basis, will turn trivial little things of monumental importance when they don't really matter at all (even if you believe things matter) such as sports. Sports is just a nearly universal accepted hobby that people love to make into a much bigger deal than it is. But then, you can find people who are like that in nearly every human endeavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that &quot;matters&quot;, but most of the people I talked about with today were religious, so to them everything you do &quot;matters&quot;, but maybe not in this life, but for the next. Granted, not everyone I talked with were real religious, it's just an observation.<br /> <br /> Not sure I'm mentally healthly or anything, but maybe I'm one of those few people who just don't care about trivial stuff...and I don't pretend anything I do is somehow super important. I have no delusions about myself or anything I do...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:00:43-08:00","id":74391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74369#post74369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yea, you spend all this time, years, trying to prove something, but once you do it, then what? You've spent years of your life so you can &quot;better&quot; at something for a small amount of time. But then what do you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically cash in on that fame for money.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason people become famous for any reason, they want the adulation of the crowd, they want the name recognition, to be recorded in the history books somewhere in some small way, and in the more immediate, they want the advertising contracts if they can swing them, the entertainment appearances, the ability to lend support to charities of choice and the possibility of getting a job that pays more because of all that hard work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74369#post74369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that &quot;matters&quot;, but most of the people I talked about with today were religious, so to them everything you do &quot;matters&quot;, but maybe not in this life, but for the next. Granted, not everyone I talked with were real religious, it's just an observation.<br /> <br /> Not sure I'm mentally healthly or anything, but maybe I'm one of those few people who just don't care about trivial stuff...and I don't pretend anything I do is somehow super important. I have no delusions about myself or anything I do...</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's a religion that gives special allowances to athletes, I really have questions for that religion.<br /> <br /> As for the trivial stuff, you can easily turn it around. What has any of us anywhere done that wasn't trivial in the long term? It's human nature, nothing we do ultimately matters, so embrace the short time that it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:05:53-08:00","id":74393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74391#post74391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typically cash in on that fame for money.<br /> <br /> It's the same reason people become famous for any reason, they want the adulation of the crowd, they want the name recognition, to be recorded in the history books somewhere in some small way, and in the more immediate, they want the advertising contracts if they can swing them, the entertainment appearances, the ability to lend support to charities of choice and the possibility of getting a job that pays more because of all that hard work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess thats something then...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74391#post74391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's a religion that gives special allowances to athletes, I really have questions for that religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no. It was a part of the conversation that was basically everything you do &quot;matters&quot; because it's all part of Gods plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74391#post74391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the trivial stuff, you can easily turn it around. What has any of us anywhere done that wasn't trivial in the long term? It's human nature, nothing we do ultimately matters, so embrace the short time that it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a way to look at it. Pretty much why I do anything really. It only matters right now...and I have to deal with conquences right now. I'd love to quit my job...but I can't because I need money and it'd just be too much of a hassle to deal with down the road.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is always the idea the past and future don't exist and only the present exists, and in that mindset everything you do &quot;matters&quot; because all there is is right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:08:19-08:00","id":74397,"title":"","content":"You've kind of touched on why it's important to them already. See, when you said the Olympics don't matter (more or less), they switched to &quot;so you're saying nothing matters?&quot;. Not a huge leap then to say that they view the Olympics, or that level of eliteness as a kind of motivator or analogue for their own lives. It's similar to why some people enjoy sports and enthusiastically follow a particular team: by going to the game, or watching on TV or whatever, they feel invested, and if the team wins, they feel (because they identify so strongly with the team, the same bits of the brain trigger) that they win, which for some can help alleviate feelings of failure or irrelevance. So, people look at people who work really hard and become the best in the world at, say skating. These people spent hours upon hours, for years, training and working, and saw a great (to them) payoff for it. But the fact is that most people, even if they did work just as hard, would never be that good. But a certain kind of mind, and there's nothing wrong with this, likes to see concrete results for effort and output. So, by latching onto examples of hard work paying off, they can feel that their hard work might pay off, which helps them to remain motivated.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my thoughts on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:28:23-08:00","id":74410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74369#post74369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that &quot;matters&quot;, but most of the people I talked about with today were religious, so to them everything you do &quot;matters&quot;, but maybe not in this life, but for the next. Granted, not everyone I talked with were real religious, it's just an observation.<br /> <br /> Not sure I'm mentally healthly or anything, but maybe I'm one of those few people who just don't care about trivial stuff...and I don't pretend anything I do is somehow super important. I have no delusions about myself or anything I do...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I also know a bunch of the religious types that think absolutely everything matters, and I'm prone to call them out to justify it within their own theology. It helps that I technically share the same general faith as most of them so they don't feel like they are dealing with someone they have to convince. They know they are dealing with the guy that challenges long held beliefs simply to get people to think about things (most of them still don't like it, especially when they are left without defenses for some of their favorite traditions, but I'm also known for being critical of my own religion).<br /> <br /> My advice on this matter, when people are trying to discuss why they think something is important keep pushing them to explain why. They'll etiher realize they don't have a good answer, that their belief is emotionally driven, or get frustrated and leave you alone about such things in the future. The third one is the most likely to happen, but sometimes it's easier to deal with such conversations when they themselves are forced to admit they don't have a good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:11:23-08:00","id":74444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74397#post74397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've kind of touched on why it's important to them already. See, when you said the Olympics don't matter (more or less), they switched to &quot;so you're saying nothing matters?&quot;. Not a huge leap then to say that they view the Olympics, or that level of eliteness as a kind of motivator or analogue for their own lives. It's similar to why some people enjoy sports and enthusiastically follow a particular team: by going to the game, or watching on TV or whatever, they feel invested, and if the team wins, they feel (because they identify so strongly with the team, the same bits of the brain trigger) that they win, which for some can help alleviate feelings of failure or irrelevance. So, people look at people who work really hard and become the best in the world at, say skating. These people spent hours upon hours, for years, training and working, and saw a great (to them) payoff for it. But the fact is that most people, even if they did work just as hard, would never be that good. But a certain kind of mind, and there's nothing wrong with this, likes to see concrete results for effort and output. So, by latching onto examples of hard work paying off, they can feel that their hard work might pay off, which helps them to remain motivated.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my thoughts on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes perfect sense to me. I suppose I can see that...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74410#post74410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice on this matter, when people are trying to discuss why they think something is important keep pushing them to explain why. They'll etiher realize they don't have a good answer, that their belief is emotionally driven, or get frustrated and leave you alone about such things in the future. The third one is the most likely to happen, but sometimes it's easier to deal with such conversations when they themselves are forced to admit they don't have a good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I try to do that sometimes. Most times, they don't have a good reason, but won't admit it. And in this case, they then just call me weird because I'm not competitive. Like I said, I guess I just have nothing to prove...not even to myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:19:15-08:00","id":74449,"title":"","content":"Why make character sheets?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:22:29-08:00","id":74453,"title":"","content":"[useless advice anecdotes begin]<br /> <br /> I'd like to think I'm a pretty detached kind of person. I adhere loosely to the Absurdist school of thought, with a dash of &quot;Nothing you do here objectively matters.&quot; My motive for doing so is actually very simple: Being free from the worry about objective worth of actions allows me to accept that there is no difference between my selfish indulgence for liking, enjoying, and accomplishing things and not doing so. It's a feeling of freedom that was borne out of the the depression that often accompanies the Absurdist/Nihilistic position.<br /> <br /> I would say, don't be concerned that people are invested in something. Be happy that they are. Get caught up in why they are, vicariously. It's a fantastic experience. Do the same with the things you love, too. None of it matters anyways, so enjoy the time you have, and don't spend so much time worrying.<br /> <br /> [/useless advice end]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:38:55-08:00","id":74470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74449#post74449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make character sheets?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I ask myself that more than you'd think.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:44:04-08:00","id":74476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74453#post74453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[useless advice anecdotes begin]<br /> <br /> I'd like to think I'm a pretty detached kind of person. I adhere loosely to the Absurdist school of thought, with a dash of &quot;Nothing you do here objectively matters.&quot; My motive for doing so is actually very simple: Being free from the worry about objective worth of actions allows me to accept that there is no difference between my selfish indulgence for liking, enjoying, and accomplishing things and not doing so. It's a feeling of freedom that was borne out of the the depression that often accompanies the Absurdist/Nihilistic position.<br /> <br /> I would say, don't be concerned that people are invested in something. Be happy that they are. Get caught up in why they are, vicariously. It's a fantastic experience. Do the same with the things you love, too. None of it matters anyways, so enjoy the time you have, and don't spend so much time worrying.<br /> <br /> [/useless advice end]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I try to do it more for people I'm close to or consider friends. Sadly the people I was talking with today are exactly friends. They're just people at work who I try to be friendly with who are sometimes nice to me....<br /> <br /> But I get what you're saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:07:50-08:00","id":74492,"title":"","content":"So you're strange. One author once said &quot;It's funny how few are like most people&quot; (not sure if he got it from somewhere else). I find strange people to the most fun to be around with and I consider myself a tad bit strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:11:21-08:00","id":74500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74492#post74492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're strange. One author once said &quot;It's funny how few are like most people&quot; (not sure if he got it from somewhere else). I find strange people to the most fun to be around with and I consider myself a tad bit strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If everyone was the same, it'd be a pretty boring place...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:12:27-08:00","id":74546,"title":"","content":"I'd feel very much in the spirit of competition. That drive to be on top, to get that gold. To get the glory! It's a high that I think most people in competitive sports understands and desires. Of course then I'd certainly want my face on a cereal box. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If nothing else, a person could get the gold, glory, and fame, and not have to worry too much about financial burden for a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T16:31:24-08:00","id":74624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74546#post74546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd feel very much in the spirit of competition. That drive to be on top, to get that gold. To get the glory! It's a high that I think most people in competitive sports understands and desires. Of course then I'd certainly want my face on a cereal box. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If nothing else, a person could get the gold, glory, and fame, and not have to worry too much about financial burden for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just don't have it in me. I'm not a very competitive person, not even against myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:47:08-08:00","id":74756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74492#post74492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're strange. One author once said &quot;It's funny how few are like most people&quot; (not sure if he got it from somewhere else). I find strange people to the most fun to be around with and I consider myself a tad bit strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, now the meaning I would derive from that quote would be that most people, at least in individualist-leaning cultures, tend to try to differentiate themselves from the crowd, and describe themselves as different and distinct, even though of course the overwhelming majority fall within the bell curve like everyone else (and just to dispel the possible snooty stink over this statement, I'm sure I do the same, and there's nothing wrong with that).<br /> <br /> But that'd just be my reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T00:19:46-08:00","id":74817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74756#post74756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, now the meaning I would derive from that quote would be that most people, at least in individualist-leaning cultures, tend to try to differentiate themselves from the crowd, and describe themselves as different and distinct, even though of course the overwhelming majority fall within the bell curve like everyone else (and just to dispel the possible snooty stink over this statement, I'm sure I do the same, and there's nothing wrong with that).<br /> <br /> But that'd just be my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you might be right, but he said it in Icelandic and translating it on the fly is perhaps not my strong suit so some of the meaning might have gotten lost in translation. The way I have always understood the meaning is that there is no average person because we are all different.<br /> <br /> The original is something like &quot;\u00dea\u00f0 er skr\u00edti\u00f0 hva\u00f0 f\u00e1ir eru eins og f\u00f3lk er flest&quot;, but I'm writing it from memory so I might be getting it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T01:31:57-08:00","id":74840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74817#post74817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you might be right, but he said it in Icelandic and translating it on the fly is perhaps not my strong suit so some of the meaning might have gotten lost in translation. The way I have always understood the meaning is that there is no average person because we are all different.<br /> <br /> The original is something like &quot;\u00dea\u00f0 er skr\u00edti\u00f0 hva\u00f0 f\u00e1ir eru eins og f\u00f3lk er flest&quot;, but I'm writing it from memory so I might be getting it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, well, if it's in Icelandic, then no, I can't necessarily derive meaning the same way.<br /> <br /> Still, kind of cool quote <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T12:06:33-08:00","id":75116,"title":"","content":"Sounds like some basic existential thinking to me. &quot;The individual is responsible for giving meaning to life.&quot; That stuff matters to those people because they make it matter and (most likely) because it was instilled within them that it is important. If it doesn't matter to you, it's because the same idea of &quot;important&quot; wasn't given to you or developed on your own.<br /> <br /> I can take or leave the Olympics. The only part I like is the curling because it's such a odd little game and is <b>SO </b>mellow by comparison. No fanfare, no tricks. Just push the rock gently and let it slide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T12:16:27-08:00","id":75127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=75116#post75116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can take or leave the Olympics. The only part I like is the curling because it's such a odd little game and is <b>SO </b>mellow by comparison. No fanfare, no tricks. Just push the rock gently and let it slide.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shakes fist*<br /> Yet another person that ignores the vital role of the sweepers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:11:33-08:00","id":75199,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the idea of the skishooting, or whatever it is called. Robin Williams once described it as a Norwegian drive-by, which is why I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:49:12-08:00","id":75234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skari-dono</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=75199#post75199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like the idea of the skishooting, or whatever it is called. Robin Williams once described it as a Norwegian drive-by, which is why I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Biathlon is the sport you're looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:11:57-08:00","id":75255,"title":"","content":"I'm going to quote my favorite Bible passage about this very thing perhaps the wisdom of Solomon will give you perspective. It's Ecclesiastes 1 and perhaps my favorite passage in the Bible.<br /> <br /> 1 The words of the Teacher, son of David, king in Jerusalem: <sup>2 </sup>\u201cMeaningless! Meaningless!\u201d<br /> says the Teacher.<br /> \u201cUtterly meaningless!<br /> Everything is meaningless.\u201d<br /> <br /> <sup>3 </sup>What do people gain from all their labors<br /> at which they toil under the sun?<br /> <sup>4 </sup>Generations come and generations go,<br /> but the earth remains forever.<br /> <sup>5 </sup>The sun rises and the sun sets,<br /> and hurries back to where it rises.<br /> <sup>6 </sup>The wind blows to the south<br /> and turns to the north;<br /> round and round it goes,<br /> ever returning on its course.<br /> <sup>7 </sup>All streams flow into the sea,<br /> yet the sea is never full.<br /> To the place the streams come from,<br /> there they return again.<br /> <sup>8 </sup>All things are wearisome,<br /> more than one can say.<br /> The eye never has enough of seeing,<br /> nor the ear its fill of hearing.<br /> <sup>9 </sup>What has been will be again,<br /> what has been done will be done again;<br /> there is nothing new under the sun.<br /> <sup>10 </sup>Is there anything of which one can say,<br /> \u201cLook! This is something new\u201d?<br /> It was here already, long ago;<br /> it was here before our time.<br /> <sup>11 </sup>No one remembers the former generations,<br /> and even those yet to come<br /> will not be remembered<br /> by those who follow them.<br /> <br /> <sup>12 </sup>I, the Teacher, was king over Israel in Jerusalem. <sup>13 </sup>I applied my mind to study and to explore by wisdom all that is done under the heavens. What a heavy burden God has laid on mankind! <sup>14 </sup>I have seen all the things that are done under the sun; all of them are meaningless, a chasing after the wind.<br /> <sup>15 </sup>What is crooked cannot be straightened;<br /> what is lacking cannot be counted.<br /> <br /> <sup>16 </sup>I said to myself, \u201cLook, I have increased in wisdom more than anyone who has ruled over Jerusalem before me; I have experienced much of wisdom and knowledge.\u201d <sup>17 </sup>Then I applied myself to the understanding of wisdom, and also of madness and folly, but I learned that this, too, is a chasing after the wind.<br /> <sup>18 </sup>For with much wisdom comes much sorrow;<br /> the more knowledge, the more grief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:36:02-08:00","id":75290,"title":"","content":"Cool enough quote, and I do agree that ultimately you cannot pursue truth <i>and</i> happiness, but minor point of fact: intelligence and education (not the same as wisdom, of course, but close enough I think for purposes of this quote) are strongly <i>negatively</i> correlated with incidence of depression, and positively correlated with life satisfaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"rea