userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:13:49-08:00","id":75592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dairugger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74410#post74410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice on this matter, when people are trying to discuss why they think something is important keep pushing them to explain why. They'll etiher realize they don't have a good answer, that their belief is emotionally driven, or get frustrated and leave you alone about such things in the future. The third one is the most likely to happen, but sometimes it's easier to deal with such conversations when they themselves are forced to admit they don't have a good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>My advice would be that when people are having a conversation about something that you don't care about, shut up and let them have their conversation. If they ask you what you think, say you're not really into that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Post edited by moderator. Darksider</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  Unnecessarily antagonistic sheeple comment. 02-20-2014, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],