><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:39:57-08:00","id":79781,"title":"","content":"And still not memorable movie quotes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 02-25-2014, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T03:43:39-08:00","id":81501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters#post74341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIt might matter to you, or a small group of people, but ultimately nothing matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you support that claim?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=74453#post74453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Nothing you do here objectively matters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think objective is the word you want there, as things objectively matter within specific contexts. If I want to keep my fish alive, it objectively matters whether I feed it or not, and objectivity is not the same as 'outside of all possible context.'<br /> <br /> Nothing empirically matters? 'Importance is not a value that empirically measured.' Well no, sociological data is considered empirical as long as it's the product of specific types of observation.<br /> <br /> 'No action or behavior matters outside of its specific frame of reference?' No, that comes too close to a tautology, as it's basically saying things don't matter because they don't matter.<br /> <br /> I can't think of a better way to say what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-28-2014, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:46:31-08:00","id":81535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/74341-nothing-matters?p=81501#post81501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you support that claim?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran across this earlier:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://files.nyu.edu/ss194/public/sharonstreet/Writing_files/Paper%209%20for%20website%20-%20Does%20Anything%20Really%20Matter%20or%20Did%20We%20Just%20Evolve%20to%20Think%20So.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Does Anything Really Matter or Did We Just Evolve to Think So?</a><br /> <br /> It's a good paper on the subject, but to cut right to answering the above question heres a quote from the end of the paper:<br /> <br /> &quot;In answer to the title\u2019s question: Nothing \u201creally\u201d matters in the sense of mattering independently of the attitudes of living beings who take things to matter, but the nice fact is that living beings evolved, began taking things to matter, and thereby made things matter.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" tar